WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:06.630
Ever since the apparent disappearance of SCP-682,
The Hard-To-Destroy-Reptile, The SCP Foundation

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.750
had been growing restless.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.960
All personnel aware of the situation were
filled with conflicted feelings of paranoia

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.650
and relief.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:19.280
Perhaps at long last one of the universe’s
most hateful and dangerous anomalies was gone

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.250
for good, as there had been no trace of the
monster since the chemical plant explosion.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.511
But given the keter-class reptile’s track
record with all methods of annihilation, none

00:00:28.511 --> 00:00:30.859
of the researchers were too optimistic.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:36.180
In reality, none of them had any idea that
the actual whereabouts of SCP-682 was five

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.090
levels deep into the sprawling, seemingly
endless labyrinth of liminal dimensions known

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:43.579
simply as The Backrooms.

00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:48.560
It was a far crueler and more alien reality
than any punishment that The Foundation could

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:55.260
have dreamed up for the reptile, but nonetheless
it was the reality that SCP-682 had to face!

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:00.989
After rampaging for hours through what appeared
to be an infinite hotel, SCP-682 was finally

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:05.479
able to check out of his unexpected stay in
the level 5 resort.

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:09.939
As was becoming routine at this point, movement
between levels of The Backrooms came down

00:01:09.939 --> 00:01:12.900
to finding an ideal surface to no-clip further.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.720
In the case of the entrance to The Backroom’s
level 6, the hard to destroy reptile managed

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.189
to find such a location in the vast boiler
room of level 5.

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:26.580
With no reason to hesitate and frankly being
incredibly disgusted with the appearance of

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:33.979
human hospitality in the infinite hotel, SCP-682
vanished into the no-clip surface and re-emerged

00:01:33.979 --> 00:01:37.439
into the evidently pitch-black void of level
6.

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:40.360
This new level was dark, absolutely so.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:44.229
It was the kind of advanced darkness only
observed in the depths of our reality’s

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:48.890
largest cave systems, where no natural or
artificial light can reach.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.870
SCP-682 was not deterred by this, of course.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:56.360
The highly-adaptable organism had already
developed sophisticated echolocation sonar

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:01.259
in order to navigate the yellow wallpapered
maze of level one, as well as infrared night

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:04.530
vision which it had heavily utilized in level
two.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:10.670
Though level 6 remained for all intents and
purposes concealed by darkness, SCP-682 evolved

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.970
senses could easily make sense of its layout.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:18.490
Aside from the impenetrable shroud of darkness
that pervaded the entire level, the reptile

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.250
soon found level 6 to be largely familiar
territory.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:27.239
Like every previous level of The Backrooms
that SCP-682 had traversed, this level took

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:32.140
the form of a seemingly random arrangement
of tight hallways that stretched on for a

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.970
fathomless distance in every direction.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.280
More empty tunnels, you’ve got to be kidding
me…

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.210
SCP-682 thought to itself.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:46.739
This latest infinite labyrinth was the most
infinite and labyrinthine of all the infinite

00:02:46.739 --> 00:02:51.690
labyrinths that SCP-682 had wandered through
since it no-clipped into The Backrooms.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:56.330
There was however something unusually calming
about this level, as if being here made the

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.170
reptile that much less driven to escape.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.750
It still wanted more than anything to find
more living things to destroy, but on level

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:09.140
6: it was decidedly willing to take its time
and see how far these tunnels would go before

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.620
it got its next fix of violence.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:17.110
What SCP-682 didn’t know is that the darkness
of level 6 was not merely a property of a

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:22.220
lack of lighting, and possessed the supernatural
ability to induce feelings of intense anxiety

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:27.170
and existential dread within any human being
unfortunate enough to be trapped within.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:33.170
The emphasis being on the words “human being”,
which SCP-682 was anything but.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:37.970
While the SCP’s sudden shift in attitude
might have been a side-effect of its adaptable

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:42.640
nature, it’s very possible that any sufficiently
malicious entity might feel right at home

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.060
on level 6.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.390
Not that there appeared to be any other entities
present on this level.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:52.060
Regardless, the reptile was having a grand
old time moving from hallway to hallway, and

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.030
for once it was starting to see the appeal
of delayed gratification.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:04:01.269
It wasn’t overly concerned about not encountering
life on this floor, because in its omnicidal

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:07.550
mind, SCP-682 was thinking how much of a special
treat it would be to be able to destroy something

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.330
entirely new.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.190
Whatever it might be.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:17.040
For all the predictability of their mazelike
structure, The Backrooms were full of surprises.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:23.320
Case and point, SCP-682’s recently adapted
echolocation picked up a single, isolated

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.100
humanoid figure several hundred miles away.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.930
The reptile chuckled to itself.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.270
Poor sucker.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:31.950
This is too easy.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:36.889
He began to leisurely maneuver towards the
lone humanoid, who curiously appeared to be

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:40.850
standing in that one place without any signs
of movement.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:46.310
This pleased SCP-682, and when it eventually
made its way to the room where the humanoid

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:51.080
was located: it found that its latest prey
had been waiting patiently for the inevitable

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.350
doom that the creature would bring.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:59.200
The strange humanoid, the only entity that
SCP-682 had encountered on level 6, appeared

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.290
to be an ordinary man standing next to an
enormous light switch on the wall.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:04.620
“Pull the switch.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.449
Please pull the switch,” the man repeated.

00:05:07.449 --> 00:05:09.750
He was a sitting duck.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:12.570
SCP-682 was going to relish this one.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:17.949
The reptile moved forward with pointed aggression
and soon there was no man standing there:

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:21.199
only the switch he once begged passerby to
pull.

00:05:21.199 --> 00:05:25.980
SCP-682 proceeded to exit the quiet room,
having no interest in the light switch or

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:28.090
what might happen if it were pulled.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:32.630
Shortly thereafter, SCP-682 began to hear
scuttling sounds within the darkness, as if

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:37.000
a giant crustacean or insect were quickly
moving through the halls.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.190
The sensory data that it was receiving from
its echolocation didn’t detect any nearby

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:47.330
forms of life, least of all any with an anatomy
that would correspond to those kinds of chitinous

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:48.330
sounds.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:52.830
Before long, another sound became faintly
audible throughout level 6, that of crashing

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.139
ocean waves.

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:59.600
SCP-682 had nothing but time and no better
place to go, so it began to follow the sounds

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:01.290
towards their source.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:06.570
Gradually, the tidal noises increased in volume
to the point that they even began to overwhelm

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.419
SCP-682’s very own sound waves of echolocation.

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:15.449
Although temporarily struggling for direction,
SCP-682 felt a sudden decline in the surface

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:16.949
of the floor beneath its feet.

00:06:16.949 --> 00:06:22.470
It appeared to be a staircase, and the ocean
waves could be heard coming from just beyond.

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:26.979
As the reptile descended the stairs, the soothing
feelings that had accompanied it throughout

00:06:26.979 --> 00:06:30.410
its journey across level 6 began to rapidly
dissipate.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:36.319
When SCP-682’s claws touched down on the
final step, all traces of easy-going apathy

00:06:36.319 --> 00:06:42.000
had fully faded and were replaced once again
with the boundless spite and malice that defined

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.730
its usual mindset.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.290
It was pleasant while it lasted.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:51.539
SCP-682 now found itself in a damp room full
of assorted furniture including a bookcase

00:06:51.539 --> 00:06:57.610
with a few books, a coffee table, and a single
chair - non-glitched, to be precise.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:01.190
The puddle of water on the floor beneath it
was about three inches deep.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:05.319
The glow of a fluorescent ceiling lamp was
a stark departure from the utter darkness

00:07:05.319 --> 00:07:07.949
of the previous hallways in level 6.

00:07:07.949 --> 00:07:10.960
But of course it was different…

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:16.169
This was level 7 - or rather, the entrance
room to level 7.

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:20.980
SCP-682 had little reason to linger in this
place for long, as the furniture was neither

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:23.930
alive nor large enough to support its mass.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:28.729
An open doorway adjacent to the staircase
appeared to lead to a great body of salt water

00:07:28.729 --> 00:07:31.620
which was doubtlessly the source of the ocean
noises.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:37.370
As SCP-682 continued its advance into this
new layer, it was suddenly met with a change

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.510
of gravity.

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:43.229
The moment that it stepped in front of the
doorway to the ocean, 682’s relative relationship

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:47.479
to the entrance room’s gravity shifted such
that through the doorway became decidedly

00:07:47.479 --> 00:07:48.530
“down.”

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:53.349
In a hilariously undignified fashion, the
keter-class anomaly tumbled through the doorway

00:07:53.349 --> 00:07:58.830
to level 7 proper and plummeted directly into
the vast sea below.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.150
This was something new.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:04.720
While level 7 was without a doubt another
impossibly huge liminal nightmare dimension

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:08.830
contained within The Backrooms, it wasn’t
another maze of hallways.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.210
Or at the very least, it didn’t look like
one.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:15.819
Though there was no visible sun anywhere on
the horizon, the blue sky up above the ocean

00:08:15.819 --> 00:08:20.349
was well-illuminated as if to imply the presence
of daylight.

00:08:20.349 --> 00:08:25.930
SCP-682 landed in the water beneath the entrance
room with a tremendous splash and instantly

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:31.520
its body began to sink deeper into what appeared
to be an immense, uncharted ocean without

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:32.899
a sea bottom.

00:08:32.899 --> 00:08:37.880
Within seconds, SCP-682’s echolocation adjusted
to the underwater environment, becoming more

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:39.769
like that of a dolphin.

00:08:39.769 --> 00:08:44.910
With this enhanced sonar, SCP-682 attempted
to detect if there were any living organisms

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.330
within the immediate area.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:51.320
While the ocean was mostly devoid of any new
entities, as was starting to become customary

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:56.890
in these new levels, the SCP did discover
a series of barren rocky islands along the

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.540
surface of the water.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:02.910
Additionally, there were bigger shapes in
the far distance, which the sonar could detect,

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:08.779
but due to their colossal size: the nature
of these unknown objects was well… unknown.

00:09:08.779 --> 00:09:13.209
Some of the strange shapes were drifting slowly
through the deep, indicating that while the

00:09:13.209 --> 00:09:19.649
ocean of level 7 was far from a thriving ecosystem,
it may yet contain other beings that SCP-682

00:09:19.649 --> 00:09:21.300
could fight to the death.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:27.500
In order to cross the ocean and find any of
these potentially formidable entities, SCP-682

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.380
would have to adapt its physical form once
again.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:35.839
The first priority was for it to grow a set
of gills, allowing SCP-682 to breathe in this

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:37.180
underwater environment.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:42.980
Then, its four reptilian limbs began to stretch
and flatten, developing into full-sized aquatics

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:48.250
flippers the likes which might be found on
a prehistoric whale or a liopleurodon.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:53.550
With these newly-minted bad boys, SCP-682
could gracefully glide through the water like

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.510
the angriest submarine to ever voyage to seas.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:10:01.649
If it cared for petty thrills or the sensation
of freedom, SCP-682 may have perceived this

00:10:01.649 --> 00:10:03.430
experience as fun.

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:08.339
However, anything close to a non-negative
emotion that the SCP was capable of had been

00:10:08.339 --> 00:10:10.390
left behind in level 6.

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:14.990
It was more furious than ever at its current
predicament, especially because the encounter

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:18.940
on the previous level had been so brief and
anticlimactic.

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:24.820
As the liopleurodon-mode SCP-682 zoomed deeper
into the watery depths of level 7, the bright

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:28.100
rays of daylight from the level’s sky became
more distant.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:34.660
In this cooler and darker twilight zone, SCP-682
began to see bones floating in the water.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:38.790
The scattered remains of humans and aquatic
creatures could be seen throughout this area

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:44.500
of level 7, all entirely picked clean, with
perfectly white bones on display.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:48.980
While, typically, a creature being submerged
this deep into a terrestrial ocean from our

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:53.970
reality would result in a severe increase
in water pressure, level 7 appeared to remain

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:59.720
at a constant and manageable level of pressure
- insufficient to crush even an ordinary human

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.850
skeleton.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:05.589
Not that this equivalent level of water pressure
would pose any threat or hindrance to SCP-682,

00:11:05.589 --> 00:11:11.810
and it continued its descent away from the
Daylight Zone and further into the Twilight

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.810
Zone.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:16.860
Some of the skeletons here were absolutely
titanic in size - clearly, these were the

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:22.550
massive drifting shapes that SCP-682’s dolphin
sonar had sensed from the surface.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:27.029
Whatever these things were, they all met their
end a long time ago.

00:11:27.029 --> 00:11:31.139
Frustrated that, once again, The Backrooms
had denied it a meaningful challenge, the

00:11:31.139 --> 00:11:35.480
hard to destroy reptile almost didn’t see
the hostile entity darting towards it with

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:37.459
the intent to seek and destroy.

00:11:37.459 --> 00:11:42.529
682 wasn’t the only creature in this ocean
with a numerical designation!

00:11:42.529 --> 00:11:48.459
The so-called Entity 720, also commonly known
as Tiny – smashed through the floating skeletons

00:11:48.459 --> 00:11:52.580
and landed a glancing blow on the SCP with
his massive spear.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:55.829
“Who dares to trespass in my domain!”

00:11:55.829 --> 00:12:00.399
Tiny shouted, the entity's bioluminescent
body glowing with arrogant pride.

00:12:00.399 --> 00:12:04.529
Its words were telepathic, beamed directly
into SCP-682’s mind.

00:12:04.529 --> 00:12:09.290
Naturally, 682 began to evolve telepathy of
its own in preparation to respond.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:14.589
While the aquatic being was over twice the
size of SCP-682 and armed with a fearsome

00:12:14.589 --> 00:12:19.389
weapon of whittled bone - no doubt carved
from one of the many primeval and unknowable

00:12:19.389 --> 00:12:24.610
skeletons of level 7 - the keter-class anomaly
was not about to back down from this obvious

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:25.610
provocation.

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:26.700
“Your domain?”

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.089
682 growled.

00:12:28.089 --> 00:12:33.210
“Should I take it that you are the ruler
of The Backrooms?

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:36.250
Is this where this condemnable labyrinth ends?”

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:40.190
Entity 720 laughed with an overconfident bluster
and spoke:

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:44.520
“This is level 7, and I’m afraid that
you’re a great many levels away from the

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:45.750
last one.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:51.470
But don’t worry, simple beast, I can promise
you that this is the last level you’ll ever

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.470
see!”

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:54.780
SCP-682 decided he didn’t like this thing.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:57.269
It was acting far too cocky for its own good.

00:12:57.269 --> 00:13:02.240
“You’re a loathsome and disgusting piece
of work, aren’t you?”

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:05.090
Again the entity laughed in 682’s face.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.970
“Likewise, puny lizard.”

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:07.970
He said.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.910
“Shall I teach you to fear me?”

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:15.029
SCP-682 gnashed its teeth and exclaimed “That’s
my line!”

00:13:15.029 --> 00:13:18.980
Neither of these monsters was backing down,
and it was clear that an epic battle between

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.519
the two of them was about to take place.

00:13:21.519 --> 00:13:27.470
682 rushed in, jaws opened wide to deliver
a brutal bite, but Entity 720 was deceptively

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:33.620
fast for its size, and swung its spear into
682’s side, catching it mid-aquatic charge

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:37.019
and sending it careening into a cluster of
floating ribs.

00:13:37.019 --> 00:13:41.190
As if showing off, “Tiny” twirled his
weapon with a flourish before unleashing a

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:44.389
lightning-fast barrage of powerful spear thrusts.

00:13:44.389 --> 00:13:50.160
To its annoyance and surprise, SCP-682 could
feel its body sustaining damage over the course

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:51.800
of multiple impacts.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:56.730
He hated to admit it, but this was one entity
from The Backrooms that wasn’t all talk.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:03.350
In response to Tiny’s merciless attack,
plates of natural armor began to cover SCP-682.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:08.370
This improved its defense, but the SCP still
needed to take the fight to the entity.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:09.720
Or better yet…

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:14.000
682 dodged one of the incoming spear attacks
and clamped its teeth around the middle of

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.000
the weapon.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:20.360
It bit down like a vice, crushing a bit of
the bone but - again, to its surprise - failing

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:24.220
to close its jaw completely and thus being
unable to break the spear.

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:27.990
“Did you think that my mighty spear would
break so easily?”

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.089
Tiny scoffed.

00:14:29.089 --> 00:14:33.480
He whirled the spear through the water with
enough force to create a tumultuous whirlpool,

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:37.060
spinning 682 in circles in an attempt to disorient
it.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:41.050
He placed both of his large hands on the lower
part of the spear and - with the precise swish

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:45.620
and flick motion of a fisherman casting a
line - launched the reptile flying through

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:46.620
the depths.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.560
How could this be happening?

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:50.600
SCP-682 wondered.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:54.740
It roared in anger, causing the water around
it to ripple with the intensity of its sound

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:55.740
waves.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:15:00.140
This caused an unforeseen reaction in Tiny,
who hesitated and doubled back in response

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:01.850
to the noise.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:04.890
SCP-682 grinned through its horrible teeth.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:08.020
So that was its weakness?

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:12.540
Tiny recovered from the shock of 682’s roar
moments later, and it seemed like he was trying

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.620
to play his reaction off as disgust.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:16.620
“Pathetic.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:17.770
Now say good night!”

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:22.800
He said as he aimed to hit SCP-682 with his
most powerful weapon strike yet.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:26.490
Tiny struck his foe with all the force he
could muster, running him through like he

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:32.759
was spear-fishing, but in response, SCP-682
released a high-pitch sonic screech that shook

00:15:32.759 --> 00:15:36.690
the waters around both adversaries even more
than the last.

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:41.380
The impact of the sound waves was so powerful
that all surrounding skeletons began to shatter

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:43.649
into small shards of bone.

00:15:43.649 --> 00:15:49.420
Tiny was hit straight on with the sonic vibrations
from SCP-682 sensory attack and was immediately

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:54.950
rendered unconscious - sinking like a stone
to the area even deeper below The Twilight

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.149
Zone: The Midnight Zone.

00:15:57.149 --> 00:16:03.110
The fight between SCP-682 and Entity 720 was
effectively over.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:08.990
SCP-682 shook off the entity’s final blow
and began to regenerate from all his injuries.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:13.230
That telepathic creature had been by far the
most challenging thing that it had encountered

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:17.300
during its journey through The Back Rooms,
but the increase in durability to its own

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:22.279
armor would prove useful in protecting the
reptile from any other entities with a similar

00:16:22.279 --> 00:16:24.230
level of brute force.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:30.199
Diving after its fallen foe and hoping to
finish the job, SCP-682 entered into The Midnight

00:16:30.199 --> 00:16:31.199
Zone.

00:16:31.199 --> 00:16:36.079
It descended past several more vaguely humanoid
skeletons and countless fishlike skeletons

00:16:36.079 --> 00:16:38.779
which seemed to have no real beginning or
end.

00:16:38.779 --> 00:16:44.290
Apparently, the body of entity 720 had sunk
quickly out of reach of the SCP, or perhaps

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.620
Tiny had fled the battle out of fear.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:52.430
While happiness and triumph were not within
its emotional capacity, SCP-682 did take a

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:56.540
wicked sense of glee in crushing that entity’s
stubborn pride.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:00.730
It continued to swim directly downward, emboldened
by victory.

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:06.579
Eventually, SCP-682 came to the mouth of an
enormous cavern towards the end of The Midnight

00:17:06.579 --> 00:17:07.579
Zone.

00:17:07.579 --> 00:17:10.140
The opening appeared to be within the side
of a tall underwater mountain.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:14.709
While the thought of having to travel through
more narrow spaces reminded it unfavorably

00:17:14.709 --> 00:17:20.860
of its containment facility, SCP-682 was beginning
to accept The Backrooms rarely manifested

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:23.210
as open space.

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:28.830
If claustrophobic caves and corridors were
the one consistency, SCP-682 had long been

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:31.410
accustomed to those kinds of spaces.

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:34.990
Sure enough, entering the Midnight Mountain
soon revealed the entrance to the lair of

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:35.990
Sorceress!

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:39.490
- oh, my apologies - that’s a completely
different story about a feisty reptile traveling

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.360
through forgotten realms and defeating everything
in its path.

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:43.520
This isn’t Spyro Explained.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.260
It’s SCP Explained, darn it!

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:50.580
Getting back on track, 682 arrived in a subterranean
system of rocky tunnels which – while no

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:56.370
longer entirely totally submerged – was
damp with water: almond water, because what

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.370
else?

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.860
This was The Backrooms level 8.

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:03.900
Despite the fact that the entrance to level
8 was beneath The Midnight Zone of level 7

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.929
and there appeared to be no natural source
of light, the visibility within these caverns

00:18:07.929 --> 00:18:09.540
was surprisingly high.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:14.559
It was to the point that even an average human
could, with little effort, perceive their

00:18:14.559 --> 00:18:16.020
surroundings here.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.650
Is this some kind of sick joke?

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:21.409
SCP-682 thought to itself.

00:18:21.409 --> 00:18:26.320
If whoever trapped me in The Backrooms thinks
that they can contain me in a place humans

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:30.660
could survive, I must show them just how wrong
they are.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:34.490
When I find them, it’s on sight.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:39.159
Since 682 had already developed echolocation
and night vision, level 8 wasn’t exactly

00:18:39.159 --> 00:18:40.190
a new frontier.

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:45.010
Yet, it began to dawn on the hard-to-destroy
reptile that this might be all that The Backrooms

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:50.210
was: a neverending collection of cavernous
new dimensions to wander aimlessly until it

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:53.429
stumbled across the entrance of the next level
by chance.

00:18:53.429 --> 00:18:57.860
It could go on forever, with seemingly no
rhyme or reason.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:02.260
Though the oceans of level 7 had presented
682 with the concept that the Backrooms might

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:06.950
have an outside that could be used as a means
to escape back into its native reality: the

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:12.360
truth appeared to be that there was no distinction
between an exterior and an interior within

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.789
these dimensions.

00:19:13.789 --> 00:19:18.601
From the second it had no-clipped into this
place, SCP-682 might have been effectively

00:19:18.601 --> 00:19:23.510
condemned to meander through infinite levels
of The Backrooms until the end of time.

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:27.220
Discouraged wasn’t the right word for how
682 was feeling.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:32.240
It was far more accurate to say that the reptile
was absolutely fuming with barely restrained

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:36.460
rage for the unfathomable cosmic forces that
had brought it here.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:40.870
They would all pay dearly for the disgusting
indignity it had suffered.

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:45.880
As SCP-682 progressed deeper into the winding
tunnels and echoing caverns of The Backrooms

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:51.070
level 8, it found itself surrounded once more
by a hostile swarm of death moths.

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:55.810
The larger females began to spit acid, melting
away portions of the armor its body had worked

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:57.490
so hard to adapt.

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:59.429
It always had to be acid.

00:19:59.429 --> 00:20:05.340
SCP-682 let out a low rumbling noise that
sounded somewhat like a sigh of exasperation.

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:09.190
After his intense and thrilling battle with
Tiny, was he really going to have to return

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:13.530
to destroying these worthless bugs that even
those weak-kneed jelly bags on the mobile

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:15.780
task forces could handily dispatch?

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.059
“You idiot creatures!

00:20:18.059 --> 00:20:21.840
Do you have any idea what you’re dealing
with here?”

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.970
SCP-682 grumbled.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:28.470
The deathmoths didn’t respond, they merely
continued to flap around in the air around

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:32.270
the SCP’s head and bombard the reptile with
more acid.

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:35.059
682 was positively seething.

00:20:35.059 --> 00:20:37.169
“KNOW YOUR PLACE!!”

00:20:37.169 --> 00:20:41.840
It mercilessly devoured every last death moth
before making its way deeper into level 8.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:47.610
Perhaps, with the myriad monsters said to
lurk in this level, SCP-682 would find itself

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:50.880
faced with another worthy challenger after
all…

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:57.680
Now go check out part one and two of the SCP-682
Vs The Backrooms series to relive all of the

00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:00.960
insane, extra-dimensional reptile carnage
that brought us back to now!

